  "ingredients": [
    "4 cups water",
    "0.25 cup kosher salt",
    "2 tablespoons brown sugar",
    "1 tablespoon cider vinegar",
    "4 pounds skin-on, bone-in chicken breasts",
    "maple wood chips",
    "1 tablespoon brown sugar",
    "1 teaspoon salt",
    "1 teaspoon ground black pepper",
    "1 teaspoon paprika",
    "0.5 teaspoon garlic powder",
    "0.5 teaspoon onion powder"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/1RHWcDcpTVpaeqBcx-D8BKeuzZc=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/272470-Smoked-Chicken-Breasts-075-step1-23de963f8c894d40af8daea25badeab5.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/272470/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make brine: Combine water, kosher salt, brown sugar, and apple cider vinegar in a large bowl. Stir until salt and brown sugar are dissolved. Place chicken breasts into brine, cover, and refrigerate for at least 4 hours to overnight.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/61AG7Wuyj-D4MMgtkW2Wak8hgqk=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/272470-Smoked-Chicken-Breasts-076-step2-4474d3ff024f45d79ca7906f7904f1b3.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/272470/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat an electric smoker according to manufacturer's directions to 225 degrees F (110 degrees C) using maple wood chips.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove chicken breasts from brine and rinse under cold water. Pat dry and set aside.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/DU39Truzltude8B0w474KH9aZC8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/272470-Smoked-Chicken-Breasts-077-step3-905f82e53a6c47e2bc8a8ea69210f22d.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/272470/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make rub: Combine brown sugar, salt, black pepper, paprika, garlic powder, and onion powder in a bowl. Sprinkle dry rub all over chicken breasts and place skin-side up on a grill rack in the preheated smoker. Place a drip pan underneath.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/7QdNAXKiSdTTs3dEpuDnVJj6rT8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/272470-Smoked-Chicken-Breasts-078-step4-aa6f3edc9a254b7797abdc5530bc8e46.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/272470/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Smoke chicken breasts in the preheated smoker until chicken is no longer pink and the juices run clear, about 4 hours, adding maple wood chips as necessary to keep the smoke continuous. An instant-read thermometer inserted near the bone should read at least 165 degrees F (74 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/A2Nx4USpee0fyEYwvjb03mAUFQY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/272470-Smoked-Chicken-Breasts-079-step5-49073c4415fb470ba6fd51cc7adb6ede.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/272470/step_06.webp"
    }
